  "result": "Reservations with expiry are now in the store and the API, and `npm test` passes (175 tests, 0 failed). I haven't committed anything.\n\n- **Store (`src/store.js`):** I added `reserve`, `confirm`, `release` and `getAvailable`, and `removeItem` now checks availability instead of physical stock. All expiry checks use the store's `clock`.\n- **API (`src/api.js`):** `GET /stock/:sku` now includes `available`. `POST /reservations`, `POST /reservations/:id/confirm` and `DELETE /reservations/:id` use the status codes you specified.\n- **Tests:** I added 6 store tests and 4 API tests covering the new behavior, including expiry at exactly creation time + `ttlMs`.\n\nI didn't add validation for `ttlMs`. A missing or non-numeric value gives a reservation that never counts as expired. Say so if you want it rejected.\n\nExpired reservations stay in memory; they just stop counting against availability.",
